import json,re,pathlib
root=pathlib.Path(__file__).resolve().parents[1]
# Editorial source: owner-supplied market research, dated 1 November 2026.
topics=[
('website-development-cost-pakistan','Website Development Cost in Pakistan 2026 (Honest PKR Breakdown)','website development cost in Pakistan','Cost Guides','web-development','How much does a website cost in Pakistan?', 'WordbitX websites start at Rs. 20,000 on your own domain and hosting, or Rs. 25,000 with a domain and one year of hosting. Market estimates are PKR 30,000–60,000 for a basic freelancer build, PKR 60,000–150,000 for a small agency, and PKR 150,000–350,000+ for an established agency.',[
('Compare scope before comparing prices','A five-page brochure and a booking platform are not the same purchase. A brochure explains your business and sends enquiries to your phone. A booking platform also stores appointments, checks availability and handles changes. Write down which one you need before requesting a price. WordbitX’s starter scope covers 5–10 pages, a CMS, basic SEO and three months of support. Confirm the final page list in your written quote. Extra languages, unusual layouts and external systems need their own scope.'),
('What the two published packages mean','The Rs. 20,000 starting price assumes you bring your own domain and hosting. The Rs. 25,000 starting price adds domain registration and hosting for one year. Do not add a made-up hosting subscription to either package. WordbitX does not publish standalone hosting plans. Renewal starts at Rs. 10,000 per year for the all-in-one arrangement. Ask which domain extension, storage limits, backup policy and renewal services are included before you pay.'),
('Why market quotes look different','A freelancer may have fewer overheads but less backup when unavailable. An agency may include planning, design review and a separate tester. Neither business model guarantees quality. Ask every supplier to price the same pages, contact forms, content entry and handover. Check whether copywriting, real photography, paid plugins and migration are included. A lower price can be fair when the scope is smaller; it becomes misleading when necessary work is hidden until launch.'),
('The cheapest advertised website','Competitors advertise websites from PKR 5,000. Offers under PKR 10,000–15,000 usually mean a copied template with weak security and no support; inspect the actual terms rather than judging on price alone. Do not assume every low-cost developer is dishonest. Ask about licensed themes, updates, backups and access ownership. WordbitX is not claiming to be the cheapest in Pakistan. Its published package is a comparison point, not proof that another supplier cannot suit you better.')]),
('mobile-app-development-cost-pakistan','Mobile App Development Cost in Pakistan 2026 (Android & iOS)','mobile app development cost in Pakistan','Cost Guides','mobile-app-development','How much does a mobile app cost in Pakistan?','Market planning ranges are PKR 180,000–600,000 for a simple app, PKR 500,000–2,500,000 for a medium app, and PKR 2,000,000–8,000,000+ for a complex app. These are market estimates, not WordbitX fixed packages.',[
('Price the complete system','The screens on a phone are only one part of an app. Many products also need an API, a database, an administration panel and notification services. A marketplace may require separate buyer and seller permissions. Specify who creates records, who approves them and who can delete them. Otherwise two developers may quote completely different products. Ask whether design, backend work, testing and store submission are included, and identify any existing system the app must connect to.'),
('Android or iOS first','Start with the phones your actual customers use, not a guess about prestige. If you already have customers, survey them or review website device data. If you have none, test a small group before funding both platforms. An internal delivery tool may only need Android devices supplied by the company. A customer app may justify both. Store account access should belong to your business, even when a developer handles the submission and release process.'),
('Cross-platform versus two native apps','Flutter or React Native can save roughly 30–40% compared with building two native apps, according to the supplied market estimates. That saving is not guaranteed for every product. Hardware features, background tasks and platform-specific interfaces may need native work. Ask for a technical reason behind the proposed stack. One shared codebase still requires testing on both operating systems. Do not accept a quote that treats two platforms as one testing task.'),
('Timeline and recurring work','A simple app commonly needs 1–3 months; a medium app needs 3–6 months. These are planning ranges, not delivery promises. App review, account verification and delayed content can change launch dates. Budget separately for server use, messaging, payment services and later operating-system updates. Keep a short first release focused on one useful workflow. A smaller working release is easier to test than a long feature list with unfinished payments and missing permissions.')]),
('shopify-store-cost-pakistan','Shopify Store Cost in Pakistan 2026 (Setup + Monthly, in PKR)','shopify store cost in Pakistan','Shopify & E-commerce','ecommerce-shopify','How much does a Shopify store cost in Pakistan?','Supplied market estimates put Shopify setup at PKR 45,000–500,000+ and running costs around PKR 8,000–25,000 per month. Basic is listed in the supplied research at $29/month, approximately PKR 8,000; check billing terms and current official pricing before subscribing.',[
('Separate setup from subscription','Setup pays for building the shop: theme configuration, collections, product entry, delivery rules and testing. The Shopify subscription keeps the platform running. Paid apps, a domain, payment processing and optional themes can add costs. Ask how many products and variants the setup quote includes. A shop with a small catalogue and cash on delivery is different from a store with subscriptions, multiple markets and a large imported inventory.'),
('Launch from Pakistan','Create the business account under an email you control. Set your store currency, legal policies, delivery zones and contact details. Check payment-provider eligibility directly rather than assuming every international gateway supports your business. Test cash-on-delivery orders, delivery charges and refunds. Confirm courier arrangements before promising nationwide delivery. Keep supplier invoices and product information ready; a beautiful theme will not fix inaccurate stock or unclear return rules.'),
('Offers without fake coupon codes','The supplied official offer is three days free, then $1 per month for three months on Basic, Grow and Advanced, applied automatically without a coupon code. Eligibility and offers can change, so inspect Shopify’s official checkout before paying. Do not buy a supposed secret code from a coupon site. A short introductory offer does not remove the normal subscription after the promotional period. Plan your budget around normal billing rather than the trial.'),
('A large market is not a sales guarantee','The supplied 2026 research counts 41,304 live Shopify stores in Pakistan, including 10,520 in Lahore. Those counts describe adoption, not the revenue your store will earn. Product quality, fulfilment, demand and clear customer service matter more than choosing a popular platform. Start with the products you can fulfil reliably. Test the order journey on an ordinary phone and check that a customer can understand delivery costs before the last checkout step.')]),
('ecommerce-website-cost-pakistan','E-commerce Website Cost in Pakistan: Shopify vs WooCommerce vs Custom','ecommerce website cost in Pakistan','Cost Guides','ecommerce-development','How much does an e-commerce website cost in Pakistan?','There is no single store price. Shopify setup market estimates are PKR 45,000–500,000+; WordbitX custom stores and software start around Rs. 2,50,000, with the actual scope quoted after discussion.',[
('Shopify: simpler platform operations','Shopify handles much of the platform infrastructure, which can reduce the work of server administration. You still need product information, delivery rules, payment checks and customer support. App subscriptions may grow as you add features. Before choosing it, list the recurring apps your workflow needs. Confirm what you can export and what must be rebuilt if you move away. Convenience is useful, but it should be an informed recurring cost.'),
('WooCommerce: control with maintenance','WooCommerce runs on WordPress and gives you control over your hosting and many store behaviours. That control comes with plugin updates, backups, security checks and compatibility testing. Free software does not mean a free operating business. Ask who will update the site and test checkout after changes. Compare the full annual cost of hosting, extensions and support with a hosted platform rather than comparing only the initial software download.'),
('Custom: only when the workflow needs it','A custom store is worth considering when existing platforms cannot support a specific business rule without fragile workarounds. Examples include unusual approvals, complex stock allocation or a connection to an existing internal system. These are scope examples, not claims about completed projects. Write acceptance tests for the unusual rule first. If a standard platform can do the job cleanly, custom development may add cost and maintenance without giving customers a better experience.'),
('Compare total cost over a full year','Ask for setup, recurring platform fees, paid extensions, hosting, support and future changes as separate lines. Do not count advertising spend as development. Do not count every sale as profit: delivery returns and payment fees matter too. A typical e-commerce build takes 4–10 weeks, depending on scope and content readiness. Choose using the order workflow and operating budget, then request comparable written quotes for the same catalogue and integrations.')]),
('seo-cost-pakistan','How Much Does SEO Cost in Pakistan? (2026 Price Guide)','seo services in pakistan price','SEO & Marketing','seo-services','How much does SEO cost in Pakistan?','WordbitX quotes SEO after reviewing the website, competition and goals. No verified fixed monthly SEO price is supplied, so this guide does not invent one. Request a written scope covering technical work, content and reporting.',[
('What an SEO quote should cover','An audit should identify crawl problems, poor page structure, slow templates and unclear content. The delivery plan should name the pages to improve and explain how success will be measured. Content planning, editing and technical fixes are separate workstreams. A cheap report that nobody implements is not the same service as making the changes. Ask who will publish updates and whether your developer needs to approve changes before they go live.'),
('Why there is no honest universal rate','A small local website may need accurate contact details and a few useful service pages. A large shop can have thousands of product URLs, filters and duplicate pages. Both ask for SEO, but the workload is not comparable. Language, competition, existing content quality and access to the website all affect the quote. Do not accept a number without knowing what work will happen during the first reporting period and what needs your approval.'),
('How long results take','Noticeable improvements usually take 3–4 months in the supplied planning guidance. New websites and competitive topics can take longer. Indexing is not the same as ranking, and ranking is not the same as receiving a qualified enquiry. Measure useful leads, relevant search traffic and technical health together. No agency can honestly guarantee the first position on Google for every buyer. Paid advertising can bring traffic sooner, but it is a different service with its own budget.'),
('What to avoid in low-cost packages','Avoid packages built around a large number of unexplained links or copied articles. Ask to see the proposed topics and the sites where any outreach will happen. Your business should own its Search Console and analytics access. Reports should explain changes in plain words, including work that did not improve performance. A responsible supplier adjusts the plan using evidence instead of promising instant results or treating a ranking screenshot as a complete business outcome.')]),
('hire-web-developer-pakistan','How to Hire a Web Developer in Pakistan (Freelancer vs Agency vs Company)','hire web developer in Pakistan','Hiring & Planning','web-development','How to hire a web developer in Pakistan?','Write a short brief, review live work, compare written quotes, confirm code and account ownership, and agree support terms before paying. Market hourly estimates are PKR 500–5,000 for freelancers and PKR 1,000–8,000+ for agencies.',[
('Freelancer or agency','A freelancer can be a good fit for a clear, limited job when you are comfortable managing decisions and availability. An agency may offer more continuity and specialist roles, but check who actually does the work. A company registration alone does not prove engineering quality. Ask how absences are covered, who reviews code and how issues are escalated. Choose the team structure that fits the project rather than assuming one label is always better.'),
('Review real work','Open a live website on your phone and try its forms, navigation and loading behaviour. Ask what the candidate built, what was supplied by someone else and whether the work is a demo. Do not treat a borrowed screenshot as proof of delivery. For a private system, request a redacted walkthrough or a practical explanation of the architecture. Respect confidentiality; a good supplier should not expose another customer’s personal data to win your project.'),
('Get the agreement in writing','The agreement should name deliverables, payment milestones, review dates, support boundaries and account ownership. Clarify whether you receive the source repository and how licensed components are handled. Ask what happens if either side stops the project. Keep domain registration under your own business identity. A small project still needs a clear written record; a friendly chat is not a substitute for knowing what you are buying and how handover works.'),
('Dedicated developers need a clear role','If you want to hire a dedicated developer in Pakistan, describe the skills, working hours, expected communication and who manages the backlog. Ask for a quote rather than assuming a published website package covers staffing. WordbitX does not publish a confirmed dedicated-developer price here. Set a realistic onboarding plan and define access permissions. Judge the arrangement on useful reviewed work and communication, not on online status or an impressive list of technologies.')]),
('wordpress-vs-custom-website','WordPress vs Custom Website: Which Is Right for Your Business?','wordpress vs custom website','Hiring & Planning','web-development','Which is better, WordPress or a custom website?','WordPress often fits editable business content; a custom build fits unusual workflows and integrations. Choose using ownership, maintenance, security and what staff must do each day, not the label alone.',[
('WordPress for content-led businesses','WordPress can suit a shop, clinic or professional business that mainly needs pages, articles and contact forms. Staff can edit content without changing code. Themes and plugins reduce some development work but still require updates and testing. Ask for a simple editor and training on the tasks you will actually use. A crowded dashboard with unused extensions can make an inexpensive site hard to maintain after the developer leaves.'),
('Custom for a specific workflow','A custom website makes sense when the work is more than publishing pages. Staff permissions, approval processes, unusual calculations and deep connections to another system may justify it. Describe those rules before choosing a framework. Custom does not automatically mean faster or safer: both depend on implementation. Ask how the application will be tested, documented and maintained. Avoid paying for a bespoke content editor when an established CMS would meet the same need.'),
('Ownership is more than receiving files','With either option, your business should control the domain, hosting account, repository and key logins. Paid themes and plugins may have licence restrictions, so ask which licences transfer and which require renewal. A custom framework may also use third-party services. Request a handover list explaining what runs where. You should be able to appoint another developer later without losing access to your own content or customer records.'),
('Think about the next editor','Imagine the person who updates opening hours or adds a service next year. Can they do it safely? Ask to try the editor during review, not only after payment. Test image uploads and small-screen layouts with realistic content. The right platform should support everyday work without forcing every typo through a developer. If the business has no internal editor, include a support arrangement rather than expecting software choice alone to solve maintenance.')]),
('custom-software-development-cost-pakistan','Custom Software (POS / CRM / ERP) Development Cost in Pakistan','custom software development cost Pakistan','Cost Guides','pos-software','How much does custom software / POS software cost in Pakistan?','WordbitX custom software starts from Rs. 2,50,000 and is quoted after scope review. Hardware, migration, integrations and support must be specified separately; the starting price is not a promise that every POS, CRM or ERP fits it.',[
('Start with the business process','Map the job from beginning to end before listing screens. A retail sale may affect stock, payments, returns and daily reporting. A CRM lead may move through assignment, follow-up and approval. An ERP can connect several departments. Each connection creates rules to implement and test. Describe who can change records and what happens when a mistake is found. That work makes a quote more reliable than simply asking for a complete system.'),
('POS needs more than a billing screen','Check barcode scanners, receipt printers, taxes, refunds, permissions and offline behaviour. A pharmacy may need batch and expiry tracking; a restaurant may need tables and kitchen routing. These are requirements to discuss, not guaranteed features in a starter quote. If FBR integration is required, confirm current eligibility, documentation and implementation responsibilities. Do not assume a generic invoice screen is compliant or that every external integration works without approval.'),
('Migration and rollout affect cost','Existing spreadsheets often contain duplicate customers, inconsistent product names and missing identifiers. Decide who cleans them and how opening balances are checked. Test the migration using a copy before moving live records. Plan staff training and a rollback route. A system that works in a demo can still disrupt trading if users are not ready. Ask for a staged rollout rather than replacing every branch and process at once.'),
('How long will a POS take','There is no confirmed universal POS timeline in the supplied research. The estimate depends on branches, devices, offline synchronisation, tax connections and migration. Ask for a phased schedule with a usable first release and explicit acceptance checks. Do not borrow the starter website timeline for business software. Request a custom software quote in Pakistan using sample receipts, reports and daily workflows, with private customer details removed before sharing.')]),
('how-long-to-build-website-app','How Long Does It Take to Build a Website or App? (Timeline by Type)','how long does it take to build a website','Hiring & Planning','web-development','How long does it take to build a website?','Planning ranges are 1–3 weeks for a starter website, 3–6 weeks for a custom business site, and 4–10 weeks for e-commerce. Simple apps commonly take 1–3 months and medium apps 3–6 months; content, review and integrations affect the schedule.',[
('A timeline includes your decisions','A build needs approved pages, accurate business information, real images and someone who can give feedback. If those are missing, the developer may produce a layout but cannot finish a useful website. Assign one decision-maker and collect content before work starts. Ask whether the quote assumes complete copy at kickoff. Delays are easier to handle when both sides know which missing item blocks the next stage.'),
('Design approval before full implementation','Review the page structure and one representative design before building every page. Changing the visual direction after implementation can mean repeating work. For an app, test the important journey in a prototype before connecting the backend. An approval checkpoint is not needless paperwork: it prevents a misunderstanding from spreading through the whole product. Keep feedback together and explain the business problem rather than sending conflicting layout requests from several people.'),
('Testing is part of delivery','Check forms, permission rules, mobile layouts, error messages and recovery paths. A store needs test orders and returns; an app needs device and platform checks. Content should be proofread in the actual layout, where long names and missing images become visible. Do not remove testing to recover a missed date without understanding the risk. A launch can be staged, with optional features postponed, while critical security and payment checks remain required.'),
('External approvals are separate dependencies','Domains, payment providers, app stores and third-party APIs may require verification or account review. The developer cannot promise how quickly another company will approve an application. Start account setup early using the business owner’s details. Track these dependencies separately from coding tasks. A useful schedule shows what the team controls and what depends on someone else, along with a fallback plan if a particular integration cannot be ready for launch.')]),
('local-seo-pakistan','Local SEO for Pakistani Businesses: Google Business Profile + Website','local seo services Lahore','SEO & Marketing','seo-services','How to rank my business on Google in Pakistan?','Keep an eligible Google Business Profile accurate, publish useful service pages, make contact details consistent and improve mobile performance. SEO usually needs months, not days; no supplier can guarantee a map position.',[
('Use an eligible business profile','Follow Google’s current eligibility and verification rules. Use your real business name, genuine address where applicable, opening hours and correct category. Do not create a fake Lahore, Karachi or Islamabad office to appear nearby. A service-area business should use the appropriate setup. Keep owner access in your own account. A profile is a business record, not a place to stuff every search phrase into the company name.'),
('Connect the profile to useful pages','Send visitors to a page that explains the actual service and service area. Include a way to call, message or request an appointment. A salon page should explain bookings; a clinic page should explain how patients contact staff without exposing medical details. Write the details a customer needs to choose. Repeating city names dozens of times does not replace clear information about what you do and where you can serve people.'),
('Reviews must be genuine','Ask real customers for honest feedback without writing reviews for them or inventing success stories. Respond politely and avoid exposing private information. Do not promise a discount in exchange for a favourable rating. Reviews can help people assess a business, but they do not fix an inaccurate address or a broken website. Track enquiries with appropriate consent and keep business information updated when hours, phone numbers or services change.'),
('Measure leads rather than only positions','Search positions vary by location, device and search intent. A report should explain relevant traffic, calls and useful enquiries alongside technical improvements. Noticeable SEO progress usually takes 3–4 months in the supplied guidance, with no guaranteed result. If you search for local SEO services Lahore, ask the supplier to explain the first tasks and access needed. Marketing and paid campaigns can complement local search, but each needs its own honest scope.')]),
('domain-hosting-cost-pakistan','Domain and Hosting Cost in Pakistan 2026 (What You Actually Pay)','domain and hosting cost in Pakistan','Hosting & Domains','web-development','How much does a domain cost in Pakistan?','Market estimates are PKR 3,000–6,000 per year for .com and PKR 2,000–4,000 per year for .pk or .com.pk. Billing periods, tax and renewal terms vary; check the registrar’s actual invoice.',[
('Domain and hosting are different','A domain is the address people type. Hosting is where the website runs. Email may be a separate service even when the domain is included. You can buy them together, but ask for each account and renewal date. Register the domain using an email you control and enable secure recovery. Losing an old developer’s email account should not mean losing the address printed on your signs and business cards.'),
('Read the annual bill carefully','A .com market estimate is PKR 3,000–6,000 per year. A .pk or .com.pk estimate is PKR 2,000–4,000 per year. Some registrars bill a longer period upfront, so compare equivalent periods. Premium names and unusual extensions can cost more and are not covered by these ordinary ranges. Check transfer terms and whether privacy or email services are extra. Save renewal notices somewhere more reliable than an unread promotional inbox.'),
('WordbitX’s included first year','The Rs. 25,000 website package includes a domain and one year of hosting. The Rs. 20,000 package uses your existing domain and hosting. Renewal starts from Rs. 10,000 per year; request the exact renewal scope in writing. There are no published standalone WordbitX hosting plans to list. Do not describe the first year as free hosting forever or assume every future service is included in the starting renewal figure.'),
('Avoid a renewal surprise','Hosts can advertise a low first-year price and renew at double or triple. Check the renewal cost, not only the signup cost. Compare taxes, backup access, migration help and account cancellation. Set reminders before expiry and keep a current payment method. If you want to use JazzCash or Easypaisa, ask the provider or WordbitX to confirm accepted payment methods on your invoice; this guide cannot promise an unconfirmed payment option.')]),
('web-hosting-cost-pakistan','Web Hosting Cost in Pakistan 2026: Shared vs VPS vs Managed','web hosting cost in Pakistan','Hosting & Domains','web-development','How much does web hosting cost in Pakistan?','Market annual ranges are PKR 1,500–15,000 for shared hosting, PKR 5,000–15,000 for WordPress hosting, PKR 20,000–80,000+ for VPS, and PKR 30,000–100,000+ for managed hosting. These are not WordbitX hosting plans.',[
('Shared hosting for modest websites','Shared hosting puts several customers on one server. It can suit a small content website when traffic and technical requirements are modest. Check resource limits rather than trusting unlimited labels. Ask about backups, restore access, supported software and support response arrangements. A low annual price is less useful if a failed update takes the business offline with no recovery route. Shared hosting is not automatically bad; it needs to match the workload.'),
('VPS means more responsibility','A virtual private server offers more control and isolated resources, but someone must configure, patch and monitor it. The market annual estimate of PKR 20,000–80,000+ does not automatically include server administration. Ask whether security updates, database backups and incident handling are included. A business owner who does not want to manage Linux should not buy an unmanaged server solely because its specifications look stronger than a shared plan.'),
('Managed hosting and WordPress hosting','Managed hosting can include operational help, but the word managed has different meanings between suppliers. WordPress hosting may add platform-specific caching or updates without covering every plugin problem. Get the actual service boundaries. The supplied annual market ranges are PKR 30,000–100,000+ for managed hosting and PKR 5,000–15,000 for WordPress hosting. Compare renewal prices, restore procedures and the support tasks you need, not just the category printed on a sales card.'),
('The cheapest hosting question','There is no verified single cheapest host in this guide. Shared hosting market estimates begin around PKR 1,500 per year, but storage, backups, taxes and renewal terms matter. Hosts can renew at double or triple the first-year amount. WordbitX includes one year of hosting in its Rs. 25,000 website package, with renewal from Rs. 10,000 per year. Standalone WordbitX hosting plans remain owner-to-confirm and must not be invented from market ranges.')]),
('website-development-discount-pakistan','How to Get a Discount on Website Development in Pakistan (Honest Guide)','website development discount Pakistan','Discounts & Offers','web-development','How can I get a discount on a website?','Reduce unnecessary scope, prepare content and compare full written quotes. WordbitX has no published coupon code here; its standard websites start at Rs. 20,000 or Rs. 25,000 with domain and one year of hosting.',[
('Save by reducing avoidable work','Prepare approved text, a service list, contact details and real photographs before requesting a build. A clear brief reduces revisions and helps a supplier quote accurately. Keep the first version focused on essential pages and a working enquiry route. Do not remove backups, licensed software or basic security to force a lower number. Ask whether optional features can wait instead of asking the developer to hide necessary work outside the quote.'),
('No invented WordbitX promo code','A coupon is only real if the business created it and will honour it. WordbitX has no confirmed coupon code to publish in this guide. The published standard prices are the offer readers can compare: from Rs. 20,000 on existing hosting or Rs. 25,000 with domain and one year of hosting. Renewal starts from Rs. 10,000 per year. No fake countdown, hidden code or invented percentage saving is needed to explain those terms.'),
('Shopify’s offer needs no code','The supplied Shopify offer is three days free and then $1 per month for three months on Basic, Grow and Advanced, applied automatically. Confirm eligibility and current terms on Shopify’s own site before you subscribe. Coupon websites often repackage such public offers as special codes. That does not prove every coupon website is fraudulent, but it means a claimed secret code may add no value. Never share your store password to unlock a discount.'),
('The cheapest honest route','A small business may need a simple website rather than a custom platform. Compare competitors’ advertised starting prices from PKR 5,000 with actual support, ownership and security terms. Under PKR 10,000–15,000 usually means a copied template with weak security and no support. WordbitX is not claiming to be the cheapest. Choose the smallest reliable scope that meets the business need and compare annual costs, not only an attractive launch figure.')]),
('ai-chatbot-cost-pakistan','How Much Does an AI Chatbot Cost for a Website in Pakistan?','AI chatbot cost Pakistan','AI','ai-solutions','How much does an AI chatbot cost?','WordbitX’s live AI service page gives an indicative Pakistan project range of Rs. 2,50,000–10,00,000. That is a broad AI service range, not a fixed chatbot package; a chatbot needs a quote covering its data, integrations, safety checks and usage costs.',[
('A useful assistant needs approved information','A website chatbot should answer from your actual services, policies and documents. Collect current information and name a person who owns updates. An assistant cannot reliably answer a refund question from a policy nobody has approved. WordbitX’s real AI offering includes internal and customer-facing assistants grounded in company documents. Start with a narrow topic and a clear route to a human when the answer is missing or sensitive.'),
('Setup and usage are separate costs','A project may need content preparation, retrieval search, integration, evaluation and a review interface. Running it can also involve model API usage, storage and monitoring. Ask for a usage assumption and a spending limit rather than accepting an unexplained monthly total. A busy support assistant and a small internal knowledge search have different traffic patterns. No verified fixed per-message price is supplied here, so this guide does not invent one.'),
('Guardrails are part of the product','Test wrong questions, missing information, malicious instructions and requests for private data. The assistant should not invent prices, offer unauthorised discounts or reveal another customer’s records. Human review is needed where an answer can cause harm or change a business decision. WordbitX’s live service describes logging, cost controls and human-in-the-loop review. Ask how those controls will be implemented for your workflow rather than treating a conversational demo as production readiness.'),
('Pilot before expanding','Choose a small set of common questions and prepare expected answers. Include cases where the correct response is to ask staff. Measure whether answers are grounded and useful before adding more documents or actions. Do not allow an early pilot to issue refunds or alter bookings without review. A successful evaluation is evidence for the next phase, not proof that the system can handle every future customer question without oversight.')]),
('ai-automation-small-business-pakistan','AI Automation for Small Business in Pakistan: What Actually Works','AI automation for small business','AI','ai-solutions','What is AI automation?','AI automation uses a model to interpret information inside a workflow, such as classifying a message or extracting invoice fields, then routes the next step. Keep human approval for important decisions and use ordinary rules when they are enough.',[
('Start with a repeated task','List work that is frequent, slow and easy to check. Good candidates may include sorting enquiries, summarising approved information and extracting document fields. WordbitX’s live AI service offers document intelligence, assistants, predictive analytics and workflow automation. These are services to scope, not a claim that a ready-made tool already solves your business. Compare the process with a simpler form or spreadsheet rule before choosing AI.'),
('Industry examples without invented results','A salon could draft replies about approved services, with staff confirming appointment availability. A clinic could route administrative enquiries without giving medical advice. A real estate team could summarise approved listing details without inventing property availability or legal status. These are possible use cases, not client results or testimonials. The first question is whether the underlying information is accurate enough for a person to approve the output safely.'),
('Protect private and financial data','Limit what the model can see and which actions it can trigger. Agree retention, redaction and access controls before connecting live records. A pharmacy, clinic or finance business may handle sensitive information that should never enter a casual public tool. Check vendor terms and the specific account settings. Do not claim that every AI subscription automatically provides enterprise privacy protections; the deployment and contract need explicit review.'),
('Choose tools by the task','There is no single best AI tool for every small business in Pakistan. Evaluate language quality, data controls, export options, integrations and ongoing cost. The existing small-business AI tools guide already covers tool selection, so this article focuses on implementation rather than creating another listicle. Run a small evaluation using examples your team understands. Expand only when you can show useful, checked outputs and a clear fallback when the system is uncertain.')]),
('can-ai-build-my-website','Can AI Build My Website? AI Website Builders vs a Developer','can AI build a website','AI','web-development','Can AI build my website?','AI builders are fast and cheap for a basic page. A developer is needed for a business website that must rank, convert and be owned outright, with reliable integrations, testing and a clear handover. AI can assist that work but does not remove responsibility.',[
('Where a builder helps','A builder can quickly produce a layout, draft copy and assemble a basic landing page. That may help test an idea or organise a first brief. Review every factual claim, image licence and contact detail before publishing. Do not let generated copy invent clients, reviews or offers. A page that looks finished may still contain weak forms, generic text or limited export options. Treat the first output as a draft, not automatic business readiness.'),
('Ranking and conversion need judgement','A useful business website needs clear service information, sensible navigation, mobile testing and a working enquiry path. Search engines need crawlable pages and honest content. A developer helps implement those requirements and check how the site behaves with real content. No developer can guarantee rankings either. The honest comparison is not human perfection against machine failure; it is whether anyone is accountable for testing, fixing and maintaining the whole website.'),
('Check what you can own','Read the builder’s export and cancellation terms. Owning a domain is different from owning an editable codebase. Some systems let you export content but not the full running application. Ask how forms, data and integrations would move if you leave. A developer-built website also needs a written ownership agreement and an account handover. Neither an AI label nor a custom label is a substitute for checking actual access and licensing.'),
('A practical combined approach','Use AI to organise questions, explore a structure or draft non-sensitive copy. Have the business owner verify claims and a developer implement and test the production site. WordbitX’s real AI services focus on assistants, documents, forecasting and workflow automation; this guide does not invent a separate AI website-builder product. Discuss web development for the website itself and AI integration only where there is a clear task and measurable reason to add it.')])
]
specific_faqs = [
 [('What is included in the starter website price?','The published scope covers 5–10 pages, CMS editing, basic SEO and three months of support. The Rs. 20,000 option uses your hosting; Rs. 25,000 adds a domain and one year of hosting.'),('How much does website renewal cost?','WordbitX renewal starts from Rs. 10,000 per year. Confirm the exact services, domain terms and invoice rather than assuming unlimited maintenance is included.'),('Is WordbitX the cheapest website developer in Pakistan?','No such claim is made. Competitors advertise from PKR 5,000. Under PKR 10,000–15,000 usually means a copied template with weak security and no support; compare actual scope and ownership.')],
 [('Android or iOS — which app should I build first?','Choose using your actual customers’ devices and required features. Cross-platform development may fit both; specialised hardware or platform requirements may justify native development.'),('Does Flutter reduce app development cost?','Supplied market guidance suggests roughly 30–40% savings versus two native apps. This is not guaranteed: native integrations, design differences and testing still affect the quote.'),('How long does it take to build a mobile app?','A simple app commonly takes 1–3 months and a medium app 3–6 months. Backend readiness, integrations, content and store review affect the final schedule.')],
 [('Is there a Shopify discount code?','The supplied official offer is three days free, then $1/month for three months on Basic/Grow/Advanced. It is automatic, not a coupon code. Verify current eligibility at official checkout.'),('How long does it take to build a Shopify store?','Use the e-commerce planning range of 4–10 weeks and request a scope-specific estimate. Product preparation, payments, shipping and custom theme work can change the launch date.'),('Does the Shopify setup fee include monthly running costs?','Not automatically. Separate setup work from the platform subscription, optional apps, domain, payments and ongoing support. The supplied running-cost estimate is PKR 8,000–25,000 per month.')],
 [('Shopify or WooCommerce — which is better for Pakistan?','Shopify reduces infrastructure work but has recurring subscriptions and apps. WooCommerce offers hosting control with update responsibility. Check payment eligibility, delivery needs and total annual costs.'),('When does an online store need custom development?','Consider custom work when a specific approval, stock or integration rule cannot be handled cleanly by standard platforms. Write the rule and acceptance checks before requesting a custom quote.'),('How long does an e-commerce website take?','A typical planning range is 4–10 weeks. Product content, payment approval, delivery rules, migration and testing affect your actual schedule.')],
 [('How long does SEO take to show results?','Noticeable improvements usually need 3–4 months and can take longer for competitive or new sites. No first-page position or number of leads is guaranteed.'),('What should a monthly SEO quote include?','Ask for the pages being improved, technical implementation, content responsibilities and useful reporting. Confirm who publishes changes, what needs your approval and which costs sit outside the scope.'),('Can an SEO agency guarantee number one on Google?','No honest supplier can guarantee every search position. Choose using transparent work, account ownership, relevant reporting and realistic timelines rather than a promised ranking.')],
 [('Should I hire a freelancer or an agency?','A freelancer may suit a limited, clear brief. An agency may provide more continuity and specialist roles. Check who actually builds, tests and supports the project.'),('What should I check before hiring a developer?','Review live work on a phone, ask what the candidate built and obtain written scope, milestones, ownership, licence and support terms. Keep business accounts under your control.'),('How much does a dedicated developer cost?','WordbitX dedicated developer pricing is Get a quote. Define skills, working hours and management responsibilities; do not apply a website package price to a staffing engagement.')],
 [('Is WordPress suitable for a small business website?','Often yes when the main need is editable service pages, articles and enquiry forms. Ask for editor training, licensed components, updates and a tested backup process.'),('Does a custom website automatically rank better?','No. Ranking depends on useful content, crawlability, performance and many other factors. Neither WordPress nor a custom framework guarantees rankings or leads.'),('Will I own a WordPress or custom website?','Ownership depends on the agreement and access. Confirm the repository, domain, hosting, admin accounts and third-party licences, including what can transfer to another developer.')],
 [('How long does it take to build POS software?','No universal confirmed POS timeline is available. Devices, branches, migration, offline sync and tax integration need a scoped delivery plan with staged testing.'),('Does a POS quote include hardware and FBR integration?','Only if the written scope says so. Confirm scanners, printers, tax requirements, external approvals and integration responsibilities separately; do not assume a billing screen proves compliance.'),('Should I buy ready-made software or build custom?','Use existing software when it fits the daily workflow and data needs. Consider custom work for important rules that otherwise need fragile workarounds, with maintenance and migration included in the decision.')],
 [('How long does it take to build a mobile app?','A simple app commonly needs 1–3 months; a medium app 3–6 months. Store review, account checks and external integrations are separate dependencies.'),('Can a website launch faster if I prepare content?','Yes, approved page content, real images and a single decision-maker remove common blockers. Confirm whether the schedule assumes content is ready at kickoff.'),('Does a launch date include testing and handover?','It should explicitly include mobile checks, forms, permissions, recovery paths and account access. Ask for checkpoints and record any external approvals outside the developer’s control.')],
 [('Does my business need a Google Business Profile?','If eligible under Google’s rules, an accurate profile can help customers find business details. Use your real identity and service area; do not create fake city offices.'),('Can local SEO guarantee a map ranking?','No. Positions vary with location, intent and competition. Measure relevant traffic and genuine enquiries alongside accuracy and technical improvements.'),('Should I create a different page for every city?','Only when the page provides genuine service information for that location. Repeated city names and fake addresses do not replace useful content or a real service area.')],
 [('Is a domain the same as hosting?','No. The domain is the address and hosting runs the website. Email may be separate. Confirm ownership, billing periods, recovery access and renewal dates for each service.'),('Is hosting included with WordbitX?','One year of hosting and a domain are included in the Rs. 25,000 website package. The Rs. 20,000 package uses your existing setup. Renewal starts from Rs. 10,000/year.'),('Can I pay with JazzCash or Easypaisa?','Ask WordbitX to confirm accepted methods on your invoice. These options are not confirmed here, and another provider’s payment methods should not be assumed to apply.')],
 [('Shared vs VPS hosting — which should I choose?','Shared can suit a modest content site. VPS offers more control but needs server administration unless management is included. Check workload, backups and support, not only memory or disk space.'),('What is the cheapest hosting in Pakistan?','Shared hosting market estimates start around PKR 1,500/year, but no single cheapest host is verified here. Check limits, taxes, backups and especially renewal terms.'),('Will hosting renew at a higher price?','Many hosts renew at double or triple their signup price. WordbitX package renewal starts from Rs. 10,000/year; confirm the current amount and scope before payment.')],
 [('Does WordbitX have a coupon code?','No owner-confirmed code is published here. Standard websites start at Rs. 20,000, or Rs. 25,000 with domain and one year of hosting. A code must be created and honoured by the owner.'),('Are coupon code websites real?','Some list genuine offers; others list expired codes or repackage automatic public offers. Verify at official checkout and never share passwords or pay a stranger to unlock a supposed code.'),('What is the Shopify no-code offer?','The supplied offer is three days free and $1/month for three months on Basic/Grow/Advanced, automatically applied. Check current eligibility and normal billing before subscribing.')],
 [('What makes an AI chatbot more expensive?','Data cleanup, retrieval search, multiple integrations, permissions, human review and evaluation increase work. Traffic and model usage affect running costs; ask for explicit limits and monitoring.'),('Can a chatbot answer every customer question?','No. It should use approved company information and hand off missing or sensitive questions to staff. Do not let it invent prices, medical advice or unauthorised discounts.'),('Is the quoted AI project cost a monthly subscription?','The live range describes indicative AI project work, not a universal subscription or fixed chatbot package. Ask separately about API usage, storage, maintenance and later changes.')],
 [('How can AI help a salon, clinic or real estate team?','It could draft approved service replies, route administrative enquiries or summarise verified listings. These are possible uses, not claimed client results. Staff must check sensitive or consequential outputs.'),('Which AI tool is best for small business in Pakistan?','There is no universal winner. Compare privacy, language quality, integration, export options and ongoing cost. The existing small-business tools guide covers selection without inventing a new ranking.'),('Does AI automation replace staff?','Not by default. Start with a repeated task, use human review where errors matter and compare against a simpler rules-based solution. Measure useful outputs before expanding access or actions.')],
 [('Can an AI builder replace a developer for a business website?','Not reliably when ranking, conversion, integrations and outright code ownership are requirements. AI can help draft or prototype, while a developer remains accountable for production testing and handover.'),('Will I own a website made by an AI builder?','Read the export, account and cancellation terms. Owning the domain is not the same as receiving an editable codebase. Check how content, forms and data move if you leave.'),('Does WordbitX sell an AI website-builder product?','No such product is claimed here. WordbitX’s live AI services cover assistants, document intelligence, predictive analytics and workflow automation. Discuss the website itself through web development.')],
]
common=[
('Write a brief that a supplier can actually price','Start with the business problem rather than a list of fashionable technologies. Explain who will use the system, what they need to finish and what happens after they submit information. Include the pages or workflows needed for the first version, the content you already have and any service that must connect to it. Remove private customer records from example files. A clear brief does not have to be long, but it should tell two suppliers enough to price the same job. If a feature is optional, label it optional rather than letting it silently become part of the essential launch.'),
('Ask for a written scope and a fair comparison','Request a quote that separates implementation from recurring services and later changes. Confirm currency, tax treatment, billing periods and what happens when a third-party provider changes its terms. Market ranges are planning estimates, not an invoice or a promise that your project will fit the lowest figure. Ask what is excluded as carefully as what is included. Compare the same deliverables across suppliers and record assumptions in one place. You can then choose a smaller first release deliberately rather than discovering after payment that important work was outside the original scope.'),
('Agree acceptance checks before work begins','Describe what a working result looks like in plain words. A visitor should be able to find the right service, submit a valid enquiry and understand what happens next. Staff should have the right permissions and a safe way to correct mistakes. Use realistic content and ordinary mobile devices during review. Check missing fields, failed requests and recovery paths as well as the happy path. These checks help both sides recognise completion and reduce arguments about whether a feature was technically present but practically unusable. Keep a short record of approvals and outstanding issues.'),
('Plan handover and ongoing responsibility','Know who owns each account, who receives renewal messages and who responds if something stops working. Request access to the relevant domain, hosting, repository and administrative tools, with appropriate security. Do not exchange passwords in public documents. Ask for a handover checklist and basic instructions for regular staff tasks. Support should explain which fixes are included and which new features need another quote. Three months of launch support is not the same as unlimited future development. Review access when a contractor leaves so that the business can keep operating safely.'),
('Choose the next step without pressure','Use the first conversation to clarify requirements, not to accept an invented deadline or an unverified discount. If a supplier needs more information before quoting, that can be responsible scoping rather than avoidance. Ask for the unanswered questions in writing and decide who will provide each answer. Keep the first launch focused enough to test and maintain. Once you have real usage evidence, prioritise the next improvements. A sensible plan makes room for uncertainty without pretending that every price, launch date or business result can be guaranteed before the work has been understood.')]
def block(t,text):return {'type':t,'text':text}
common.append(('Check the real cost after the first year', 'Before making a decision, create a simple list of everything that renews: domains, hosting, subscriptions, extensions and any agreed maintenance. Record who pays each bill and what happens if you cancel. Ask whether the introductory rate changes at renewal and whether you can export your content and records. Keep copies of invoices and the agreed scope with the business owner. This makes it easier to compare an inexpensive first year with a more stable ongoing arrangement. Do not assume an included launch service remains included forever. A clear renewal record is more useful than a sales promise that does not identify the service, period or responsible provider.'))
editorial=json.loads((root/"src/lib/guide-editorial.json").read_text())
posts=[]; faqrows=[]
for i,(slug,title,kw,cat,service,q,a,sections) in enumerate(topics):
    related=[topics[j][0] for j in range(len(topics)) if j!=i and topics[j][3]==cat]
    related += [s for s in ['website-development-cost-pakistan','domain-hosting-cost-pakistan','hire-web-developer-pakistan'] if s!=slug and s not in related]
    extras={'AI':['best-ai-tools-small-business'],'SEO & Marketing':['seo-vs-google-ads'],'Shopify & E-commerce':['ecommerce-website-cost-pakistan','shopify-vs-woocommerce'],'Hosting & Domains':['website-development-cost-pakistan'],'Discounts & Offers':['website-development-cost-pakistan','shopify-store-cost-pakistan','domain-hosting-cost-pakistan']}
    if cat in extras:
        same=[t[0] for t in topics if t[0]!=slug and t[3]==cat]
        related=list(dict.fromkeys(same+extras[cat]+related))
    related=related[:3]
    link='/blog/'+slug
    faqs=[{'question':q,'answer':a,'href':link},
      {'question':f'What should I include in a {"project" if cat=="AI" else "website or software"} quote request?','answer':f'Describe the first useful release, who uses it, the content available and any integrations. Ask for exclusions, recurring costs and handover terms before approving {kw}.','href':'/services/'+service},
      {'question':'Are these fixed WordbitX prices or market estimates?','answer':'Only the explicitly named WordbitX starting prices are published company prices. Other ranges are supplied market planning estimates dated 1 November 2026. Request a written quote for your scope.','href':'/pk'},
      {'question':'What should I check about support and ownership?','answer':'Confirm code and account access, licence terms, backup responsibility and renewal dates. WordbitX’s published website scope includes three months of support; agree the boundaries and any later care work in writing.','href':'/pricing'}]
    faqs=[faqs[0]]+[{'question':question,'answer':answer,'href':link} for question,answer in specific_faqs[i]]
    blocks=[block('p',f'This guide explains {kw} in simple English for a business comparing practical options in Pakistan. The aim is to help you ask better questions before buying, not to promise the lowest price or guaranteed results. The market figures were supplied for an editorial review dated 1 November 2026. Provider terms, currency conversion and taxes can change, so confirm the final written quote before paying.'),block('h2','The short answer'),block('p',a)]
    for h,p in sections:blocks.extend([block('h2',h),block('p',p)])
    for h,p in common:blocks.extend([block('h2',h),block('p',p)])
    blocks.extend([block('h2','Where to go next'),block('p',f'Discuss [{kw}](/services/{service}) with a clear brief, compare the [published Pakistan packages](/pk) and read the [pricing approach](/pricing). For the next decision, see [{next((t[1] for t in topics if t[0]==related[0]),related[0].replace("-"," "))}](/blog/{related[0]}) and [{next((t[1] for t in topics if t[0]==related[1]),related[1].replace("-"," "))}](/blog/{related[1]}). The [full question hub](/faqs) brings together hosting, timelines, platform choices and hiring checks. You do not need to decide on every future feature before asking for a sensible first-phase quote.')])
    if slug=='how-long-to-build-website-app': blocks.append(block('p','For an app-specific scope, discuss [mobile application development](/services/mobile-app-development) alongside the web work.'))
    if slug=='local-seo-pakistan': blocks.append(block('p','If you need a wider acquisition plan, compare [digital marketing services](/services/digital-marketing) separately from organic local search.'))
    if slug=='can-ai-build-my-website': blocks.append(block('p','See the actual [AI integration services](/services/ai-solutions) before assuming any AI website-builder product is included.'))
    post=dict(slug=slug,title=title,h1=title,category=cat,excerpt=a,metaTitle=title,metaDescription=a[:155],keywords=[kw],publishedAt='2026-11-01',updatedAt='2026-11-01',readingMinutes=8,author={'name':'WordbitX Editorial Team','role':'Software & Digital Solutions','bio':'Practical buying guidance based on published WordbitX services and owner-supplied market research, reviewed 1 November 2026.'},image='/guides/'+slug+'.png',imageAlt='Actual WordbitX '+('AI services' if cat=='AI' else 'Pakistan pricing')+' page screenshot; not a client result',blocks=blocks,relatedServices=list(dict.fromkeys([service]+(['ai-solutions'] if cat=='AI' else (['mobile-app-development'] if slug=='how-long-to-build-website-app' else (['digital-marketing'] if slug=='local-seo-pakistan' else []))))),relatedPosts=related)
    edit=editorial[slug]
    post['metaDescription']=edit['description']
    if edit.get('generated'):
        post['image']='/guides/'+slug+'.webp'
        post['imageAlt']=edit['alt']
    posts.append(post);faqrows.append({'slug':slug,'faqs':faqs})
(root/'src/lib/guides-2026.json').write_text(json.dumps(posts,indent=2,ensure_ascii=False)+'\n')
(root/'src/lib/guide-faqs.json').write_text(json.dumps(faqrows,indent=2,ensure_ascii=False)+'\n')
for p,f in zip(posts,faqrows):
    words=sum(len(b.get('text','').split()) for b in p['blocks'])+sum(len(x['question'].split())+len(x['answer'].split()) for x in f['faqs'])
    print(p['slug'],words)
